Resolve every downward API env fieldRef the kubelet supports.

The virtual kubelet resolved env fieldRefs itself and knew only status.podIP,
metadata.name, metadata.namespace, metadata.uid, and single annotations. Any
other path, such as metadata.labels['topology.kubernetes.io/region'] or
spec.nodeName, became an empty string, so a remote container could not read
the node topology labels Kubernetes copies onto the pod. resolveEnvRefs now
uses the same resolver as downward API volumes, which also accepts single
label and annotation references; like the kubelet, a missing key resolves to
the empty string. A path that resolver does not support is logged and left
unresolved instead of being blanked.

Upstream status: not yet reported to interlink-hq/interLink.

